  "notes": "Agent re-read 2026-11-08. THM-0136's own claim is byte-identical; its fingerprint moved through THM-0101's corrected claim (verification/claim-corrections/THM-0136-thm-0101-refusal-route-2026-11-04.json) and through supporting-unit changes. Read since the last record (ab5f4f4ff): success_exit.rs calls permit.withdraw() where it called permit.exchange(), which gives the exchange back to the refusal and consumes the permit, so a refused success cannot then publish; the outcome-commitment path is otherwise unchanged. posture.rs renamed pre_dispatch_wait to commitment_waits and the crossing's wait now covers both G1 and G2 (#1224, the signing window must survive the outcome commitment's wait): a timing budget, not an order or a posture re-read, and the claim's outcome-before-success order, redeemed witness and refusal on failure are untouched; the witness tests moved into a shared redeem_for helper with the same inputs and expected refusals. outcome_before_success_test and the exchange ownership controls pass. The order evidence is as the owner ruling of 2026-10-29 left it (type order, S81, M616-M618); its mutation and structural probes were not re-measured here. Conclusion: the claim holds. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Nothing under verification/claim-corrections/ is edited; the correction records stay as the history, and a correction record is not an approval. Evidence class as registered: the V0 units are tested, mutation-probed and structurally probed, not machine-checked proofs. No mutation, SDK-matrix or Verus lane was run for this record; the cited tests named below were run through Bazel and pass.\n\nEarlier record notes (still the provenance of the earlier readings, reviewer then: agent:claude-opus-5-5 (owner ruling of 2026-10-29 on #1263; prepared for owner ratification, not an owner signature)): Agent re-review for epic #1201 (ADR-MCPRE-070), prepared under the owner's directive of 2026-10-21 transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/epic-1201-authority-closure-2026-10-21.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only, and the owner's ratification is the ledger line that ruling file names, which does not exist when this record is written.  Re-read after the owner directions of 2026-10-21 were applied (packet section 'Addendum 2'): its identity moved after the packet's 11d940f9 measurement only through test_sources, from one added test, outcome_before_success_test.rs::required::a_window_that_lapses_during_g2_is_refused_by_the_client_never_accepted (ADR-MCPRE-070 O5); no test or assertion was removed or weakened, and the reading is unchanged. Its root edge is not taken: the proposed edge is THM-0078 depends_on THM-0136 (direction 5), awaiting the owner. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. Re-recorded under the owner ruling of 2026-10-29 on #1263 (verification/reviews/rulings/thm-0136-exit-order-2026-10-29.md), which approves the specification correction at this fingerprint, preserving its stated V0 evidence limitations. Its claim moved (bc2ba3a5 -> 5c0bebe9): the scope drops \"an absent coordinate\" from the failure list and states that the exit's order is held by types (Committed/Retained, structural probe S81) while the uniqueness of the success exit is measured from source, not enforced by the compiler; its THM-0101 dependency digest moved through the correction the owner accepted on 2026-10-27. Its supporting semantics gained proxy.success_exit_order (#1264) and moved through #1253-#1265: source_inputs of the five audit units, proxy.audit_intent_gate_sole_producer structural_probes, proxy.audit_outcome_gate mutation_probes, test_selection and test_sources, proxy.audit_posture test_sources. Premises unchanged. Evidence class as registered: V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs.",
